{'symbol': 'LEG', 'date': '2019-11-05 22:30:00', 'title': 'Leggett & Platt, Incorporated Announces Dividend for the Fourth Quarter, Payable on January 15, 2020; Elects Mary Campbell as Director', 'text': "Leggett & Platt's Board of Directors announced a dividend of $0.40 per share for the fourth quarter, an increase of $0.02 per share or 5.3% versus the fourth quarter of 2018. The dividend will be paid on January 15, 2020 to shareholders of record on December 13, 2019. In addition, Leggett & Platt announced the election of Mary Campbell to its Board of Directors effective immediately. Ms. Campbell, 52, serves as Chief Merchandising Officer of Qurate Retail Group and Chief Commerce Officer of QVC U.S.Ms. Campbell currently serves as a director of the Accessories Council."}
{'symbol': 'LMT', 'date': '2019-11-05 22:30:00', 'title': 'Lockheed Nets $40.3 Million Contract for Trident II Production, Support', 'text': "Lockheed Martin Space has been awarded a contract modification for work on submarine-launched intercontinental ballistic missiles, part of the nation's nuclear triad. The $40.3 million contract, announced 04 November 2019 by the Department of Defense, covers production and deployed systems support for the Trident II D5 and is the latest in a string of contracts for the missiles issued to Lockheed this year. The Lockheed division received a $494.8 million modification under the same contract for production and support on the Trident II at the end of September as part of ongoing upgrades and improvements to the missile system. The Trident II D5 ICBM is used for the sea-based portion of the United States' nuclear capability. The other legs of the triad are launched from either air or land. The Trident II D5 ICBM, first deployed by the Navy in 1990, is a three-stage, solid-fuel, inertially guided missile that can travel as far as 4,000 nautical miles and deliver varying numbers and multiple types of reentry bodies, according to the Navy. The Navy has obligated the full value of the contract from fiscal 2020 weapons procurement and other procurement funds, with work under the modification expected to be completed by Sept. 30, 2024."}
{'symbol': 'MAR', 'date': '2019-11-05 20:30:00', 'title': 'Marriott International Posts Q3 EPS Of $1.16', 'text': 'MARRIOTT INTERNATIONAL REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.47.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.16.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.49 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.MARRIOTT - FOR FULL YEAR 2019, WE EXPECT CASH RETURNED TO SHAREHOLDERS THROUGH DIVIDENDS AND SHARE REPURCHASES COULD APPROACH $3 BILLION.MARRIOTT - Q3 COMPARABLE SYSTEMWIDE CONSTANT DOLLAR REVPAR ROSE 1.5% WORLDWIDE, 1.9 PERCENT OUTSIDE NORTH AMERICA AND 1.3 PERCENT IN NORTH AMERICA.MARRIOTT - FOR Q4 OF 2019, WE EXPECT COMPARABLE REVPAR ON A CONSTANT DOLLAR BASIS WILL INCREASE 0 TO 1 PERCENT IN NORTH AMERICA.MARRIOTT - QTRLY TOTAL REVENUES $5,284 MILLION VERSUS $5,051 MILLION.MARRIOTT SEES 2020 COMPARABLE SYSTEMWIDE REVPAR ON CONSTANT DOLLAR BASIS WILL BE FLAT TO UP 2% WORLDWIDE WITH INCREASE IN NORTH AMERICA IN MIDDLE OF RANGE.MARRIOTT - ANTICIPATES ITS GLOBAL NET ROOMS GROWTH RATE IN 2020 WILL BE COMPARABLE TO ITS EXPECTATION FOR 2019.MARRIOTT - COMPANY ASSUMES FOURTH QUARTER 2019 GROSS FEE REVENUES WILL TOTAL $960 MILLION TO $970 MILLION.MARRIOTT - ANTICIPATES GLOBAL NET ROOM ADDITIONS OF 5.0 TO 5.25 PERCENT FOR FULL YEAR 2019.MARRIOTT - COMPANY EXPECTS FULL YEAR 2019 GROSS FEE REVENUES WILL TOTAL $3,809 MILLION TO $3,819 MILLION.MARRIOTT - ANTICIPATES FULL YEAR 2019 DILUTED EPS COULD TOTAL $5.87 TO $5.90.MARRIOTT - EXPECTS FULL YEAR 2019 GENERAL, ADMINISTRATIVE, AND OTHER EXPENSES COULD TOTAL $921 MILLION TO $926 MILLION.'}
