{'symbol': 'TPR', 'date': '2019-11-05 10:30:00', 'title': 'Tapestry Reports Q1 Earnings Per Share $0.07', 'text': "TAPESTRY, INC. REPORTS FISCAL 2020 FIRST QUARTER RESULTS.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.07.Q1 SALES $1.36 BILLION VERSUS $1.38 BILLION.QTRLY COACH GLOBAL COMPARABLE STORE SALES INCREASED 1%.QTRLY NET SALES FOR KATE SPADE TOTALED $306 MILLION COMPARED TO $325 MILLION.QTRLY KATE SPADE GLOBAL COMPARABLE STORE SALES DECLINED 16%.INVENTORY WAS $880 MILLION AT THE END OF QUARTER.QTRLY NET SALES FOR COACH TOTALED $966 MILLION 1% ABOVE PRIOR YEAR.EXPECTS REVENUES FOR FISCAL 2020 TO INCREASE AT A LOW-SINGLE-DIGIT RATE.SEES FY EPS TO BE APPROXIMATELY EVEN WITH PRIOR YEAR.STUART WEITZMAN SALES FOR QUARTER WERE NEGATIVELY IMPACTED BY SOFTER WHOLESALE DEMAND AND CONTINUED OPERATIONAL CHALLENGES.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.55, REVENUE VIEW $6.14 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.MAINTAINING OUR OUTLOOK FOR FISCAL 2020.TAPESTRY - KATE SPADE'S COMPARABLE STORE SALES DECLINED IN QUARTER, REFLECTING PRODUCT AND MERCHANDISING CHALLENGES PREVIOUSLY IDENTIFIED.ON COACH, COMPS IN QUARTER IN EUROPE, JAPAN, CHINA WERE STRONG OFFSETTING WEAKNESS IN HONG KONG; NORTH AMERICA WAS EVEN WITH PRIOR YEAR.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.37, REVENUE VIEW $1.37 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.40."}
{'symbol': 'TPR', 'date': '2019-11-05 22:30:00', 'title': 'Tapestry, Inc. Provides Earnings Guidance for Second Quarter and Full Year 2020', 'text': 'Tapestry, Inc. provided earnings guidance for second quarter and year 2020. The Company expects revenues for Fiscal 2020 to increase at a low-single-digit rate from Fiscal 2019. In addition, the Company projects earnings per diluted share to be approximately even with prior year.Starting with the second quarter, the company is projecting revenue to be similar to prior year. This guidance incorporates continued low single-digit comp growth at Coach. Operating income is expected to decline in the quarter due to a contraction in gross margin as well as mid-single-digit increase in SG&A growth, including the shift in timing of expenses from the first quarter. The company expects earnings per share to be $0.95 to $1 in second quarter.'}
